    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d700">

                <pb facs="0926" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/8441: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-30T19:00:00-06:00">May 30, 1936—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>153. Referring to first paragraph, section 2, Department’s telegram No.
                        72,<anchor n="73" xml:id="d700-f1"/> President Sacasa and General Chamorro
                    have no knowledge of any arms coming from the United States for the purposes
                    indicated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d700-f1" n="73" xml:id="d700-f1-content">
                <p>May 29, 5 p.m., <ref target="#pg824">p. 824</ref>; reference, apparently, is to
                    second paragraph of telegram.</p>
            </note>
